# Publication and reuse policy

## Repository visibility

The repository is intended to be publicly readable when the owner changes
visibility to Public. Publication does not mean every branch is stable.

## License status

State the license decision explicitly. Example (no license granted):

> This project is intentionally published without an open-source license.
> All rights are reserved by the applicable rightsholders. Public visibility
> does not grant permission to use, modify, redistribute, sublicense, or sell
> the code or documentation.

Replace the paragraph above if you choose MIT, Apache-2.0, or another license,
and add a root `LICENSE` file that matches that decision.
